'Hard West' should be a real treat for all TBS fans, and especially for those who wanted something similar ever since they finished Desperados - Wanted Dead or Alive, all those years ago.
Pluses
-Solid XCOM in the Wild West formula, spiced up by some supernatural abilities;
-Fun combat, plenty of special abilities;
-Poker-style card powerups are a nice idea;
-Awesome narration;
-Great texts;
-Lots of fun little things to discover on the strategic map;
-Each scenario comes with its own particuliarity, gameplay-wise.
Minuses
-Good soundtrack, but slightly repetitive;
-Some scenario endings feel very abrupt;
-Some problems with the cover system and afferent damage dealt;
-Unclear benefits of some optional objectives.
Overall: Very good

I just love Mafia series, I have played all three games now and what can I say, it has some good and bad aspects:
Pros:
- Amazing music soundtrack;
- Appealing time period;
- Good story;
- Rememberable main characters;
- Satisfying gun gameplay.
Cons:
- Poor optimization;
- Mediocre graphics;
- Awful AI;
- Repetitiveness (where you do the same things in all the districts);
- Empty open world (you still don't have much to do in the game and where to spend the money on, expept guns and upgrades);
+I am angry because Hanger 13 (or maybe 2K) spoiled story plots in video trailers! This is unexceptable!
Still I hope that Mafia 3 will succeed so game will be fixed and improved upon in the future.
